  "finalReply": "Created polyglot script at `/app/polyglot/stats.sh.py` (executable).\n\n**Polyglot mechanism:**\n- `#!/bin/bash` + `\"\"\":\"` is a `:` no-op in bash, but opens a triple-quoted string in Python hiding the bash block; `\":\"\"\"` closes it. Bash `exit 0` prevents reaching Python code.\n- Bash path uses `awk` (lines/words/lowercasing), `sort | uniq`, `wc`, `tr`; Python path uses `open` + `re.findall` + `lower()` + `set`.\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Lines via `awk END{print NR+0}` / Python `for line in f` with `newline='\\n'` (both count `\\n`-separated records, including final partial line; empty → 0).\n- Words via `awk NF` / Python `re.findall(r'[^ \\t\\n]+')` — narrow space/tab/newline definition so `\\r/\\f/\\v` handling is identical.\n- Unique via `tolower` + `sort|uniq|wc -l` / Python `w.lower()` set.\n- Streaming line-by-line (no whole-file read); `open(..., errors='replace')` for robustness.\n- Wrong arg count, missing/unreadable/directory → stderr + exit 1. Output is exactly `Lines: N\\nWords: N\\nUnique: N\\n`.\n\n**Verified:**\n- `bash` vs `python3` identical on: empty, basic, no-trailing-newline, whitespace-only, mixed-case/punctuation, consecutive whitespace, single `\\n`, single char, embedded empty lines, `\\r/\\f/\\v`, CRLF, 200k-line file, error cases (missing file, 0/2 args, directory); `od -c` confirms exact 3-line newline-terminated format.",
